# A bare return at the level that opens an ordinary named Structure (no fn, no sub) adds the return to the end of its body and closes its Frame
# (the grammar, section 17): the dump prints it as the last statement of Point, and the Structure is run by call.
sub: main () (
    Point:
        int: x 3
        int: y 0
        y := x + 4
    return
)
    call: Point
main()
